{
  "info": {
    "name": "SWENG 861 Week 3 - Coverages API",
    "description": "Every endpoint of the Week 3 service, exercised through the gateway.\n\nSETUP\n1. Start the stack:   docker compose up -d\n2. Seed and get tokens:   .venv/bin/python seed_demo.py\n3. Paste the three tokens into tokenA, tokenB and tokenAdmin.\n4. Run the collection.\n\nThe tokens are collection variables with empty defaults, and they are meant to stay empty in the committed file. A bearer token pasted into a file that is pushed is a credential published to whoever reads the repository, and these expire in an hour anyway - re-running seed_demo.py is the intended way to get a fresh pair.\n\nRequests carry assertions rather than being sent by hand, so a run produces a pass/fail table. That is better evidence than a screenshot of one green response: it states what each response was supposed to be before it arrived.\n\nbaseUrl points at the gateway on :8000, which is the only way in. The API publishes no host port, so there is no path that bypasses it.\n\nAI use: drafting and test-case enumeration.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "description": "The gateway. The API container publishes no port of its own."
    },
    {
      "key": "tokenA",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Analyst A's session token, from seed_demo.py. Left empty on purpose."
    },
    {
      "key": "tokenB",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Analyst B's session token, from seed_demo.py. Left empty on purpose."
    },
    {
      "key": "tokenAdmin",
      "value": "",
      "description": "The administrator's session token, from seed_demo.py. The role is a column on that user's row, not a claim in this token."
    },
    {
      "key": "idA",
      "value": "1",
      "description": "Analyst A's Apple coverage. seed_demo.py restarts the id sequence, so this is stable across re-seeds."
    },
    {
      "key": "idB",
      "value": "4",
      "description": "Analyst B's Apple coverage - the same filer as idA, held by the other tenant."
    },
    {
      "key": "createdId",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set at runtime by the create request in folder 3."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Health",
      "description": "The gateway answers without reaching the API, so a failure here separates \"the gateway is down\" from \"the API is down\".",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "health (no token)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Unauthenticated on purpose: a health check that needed a token could not be used by the container runtime."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "pm.test(\"reports the service is up\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql(\"ok\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
