            },
            "description": "200 rather than 201: nothing is created at a new URL. The POST is an action that reaches another system and returns a report of what it stored - a count and the tags it came from, not the rows. Returning sixty rows from a POST would make the body grow with the filer's history for no reason the caller stated."
          },
